scope: |
  `List.fill` / `List.tabulate` / `List.range` — the List COMPANION, which v3 does not have.
  Measured, not assumed: `List` is 4 of the corpus's `unknown name` refusals, and the shapes it is
  asked for are `List.fill(4)(0)`, `List.tabulate(5)(i => i*i)`, `List.range(1,6)` and
  `List.range(0,10,3)`.

  IN THE PRELUDE, IN ScalaScript — not in the kernel. The project's own rule is that new intrinsics
  go to a library and never to the core, and a library written this way reaches BOTH lanes with no
  host surface at all. Probed before claiming: an `object List` coexists with the `List(…)` literal
  constructor, which `Lower` special-cases, because one is the name `List` and the other is
  `List.fill` — different entries in `sigs`.

  NARROW: one file. No kernel, no gate script, no board.
